# React Components

- Use functional components only; no class components
- Define explicit props interfaces (suffix `Props`); export when reused
- Split presentational (UI) from container (data/logic) when a component grows beyond ~80 lines
- Colocate styles in `{Name}.css.ts`; never use inline `style={{}}` or CSS modules
- Prefer composition over prop drilling; extract custom hooks for reusable logic
- Keep components focused — one primary responsibility per file
- Use `children` and render props sparingly; prefer explicit props for clarity
- Default exports only in route/page files; named exports elsewhere

```tsx
// Pattern
export function UserCard({ user, onEdit }: UserCardProps) {
  return (
    <Card className={styles.card}>
      <Typography.Text>{user.name}</Typography.Text>
    </Card>
  );
}
```

For good/bad examples, read `examples/rules/react-components.md` when applying this rule.
